# File: specs/feature-remove-the-automated-sdlc-loop-and-unattended-mode/feature.gherkin
# Generated from: specs/feature-remove-the-automated-sdlc-loop-and-unattended-mode/requirements.md
# Issue: #151

Feature: Remove the automated SDLC loop and unattended mode
  As a developer using nmg-sdlc's interactive, spec-driven workflow
  I want the plugin to provide only the manual SDLC pipeline
  So that its product surface stays focused on the workflow that provides value with current AI models

  Scenario: Fresh install has no automated loop surface
    Given a user installs a published nmg-sdlc v2 artifact into a new isolated project
    When the active installed skills, scripts, configuration templates, tests, and packaged metadata are inventoried
    Then no automated loop, runner configuration, runner lifecycle, or stop-loop capability is present
    And no compatibility stub, alias, redirect, or deprecation surface exposes a removed command
    And the evidence identifies the installed version, source commit, and active plugin root

  Scenario: Skills use interactive contracts only
    Given a surviving SDLC skill reaches a decision or review gate
    And a stale file named ".codex/unattended-mode" may exist in the project
    When the skill runs after the v2 removal
    Then it waits for explicit user input through its interactive human-judgment contract
    And no plugin sentinel, unattended default, automatic approval, escalation branch, or orchestrator handoff changes that behavior

  Scenario: Automation eligibility is absent from issue workflows
    Given a repository has issues with and without an existing "automatable" label
    When a user drafts a new issue and manually selects work
    Then the plugin does not ask whether an issue is suitable for automation
    And it does not create, apply, filter by, remove, or display the "automatable" label
    And existing repository labels and issue-label assignments remain unchanged

  Scenario: Active product surfaces describe only the manual pipeline
    Given current plugin metadata, documentation, steering, templates, references, agents, fixtures, inventory, and skill output
    When the active plugin-surface validator inspects those contracts
    Then they describe only the interactive pipeline from issue drafting through review-comment handling
    And no runnable automated-loop command, asset, alias, stub, or current capability claim remains
    And an injected active automation token produces a deterministic violation

  Scenario: Managed repository assets remain available
    Given a new project is onboarded or an existing project is upgraded
    When nmg-sdlc applies its managed repository contracts
    Then the contribution-check workflow can be installed or reconciled
    And the structured GitHub issue form can be installed or reconciled
    And neither asset depends on init-config or runner configuration
    And unrelated workflows and issue templates are preserved

  Scenario: Upgrade removes only known obsolete runner artifacts
    Given an existing project contains nmg-sdlc-owned runner files, recognized managed ignore entries, and unrelated user content
    When the user approves the v2 cleanup proposed by upgrade-project
    Then sdlc-config.json is removed when present
    And .codex/unattended-mode is removed when present
    And .codex/sdlc-state.json is removed when present
    And only exact entries inside recognized nmg-sdlc runner-ignore blocks are removed
    And managed repository assets and unrelated user content are preserved
    And a repeated migration reports an already-clean state without another diff

  Scenario: Existing GitHub labels and issue history are not mutated
    Given an existing repository has an "automatable" label and issues carrying that label
    When nmg-sdlc v2 is installed or upgrade-project applies the v2 migration
    Then no GitHub label deletion command is issued
    And no existing issue label is edited
    And the plugin simply stops creating or consuming the metadata

  Scenario: Historical records remain truthful and intact
    Given historical specs and released changelog entries document automation features from earlier versions
    When active automation contracts are removed and the plugin surface is validated
    Then the historical files remain unchanged
    And the validator excludes those declared historical sources from active capability findings
    And negative regression fixtures cannot be discovered as runnable plugin behavior

  Scenario: Conflicting backlog is reconciled
    Given issues 144, 145, and 149 previously included runner or unattended-mode context
    When their live GitHub state and delivered contracts are reviewed for the v2 removal
    Then each issue is closed as superseded or its delivered behavior is validly manual-only
    And status remains a read-only manual utility
    And epic membership remains non-blocking coordination for manual consumers
    And no open backlog item continues to require removed automation behavior

  Scenario: Manual pipeline and migration are verified
    Given the v2 removal and migration have been implemented
    When inventory checks, repository tests, migration exercises, and a disposable manual pipeline exercise run
    Then no active automation contract or packaged runner asset remains
    And migration proves owned deletion, unrelated-content preservation, and idempotence
    And the interactive pipeline works from issue drafting through review-comment handling
    And local fixture success is reported separately from published fresh-install and upgrade proof
